  v2.1.7 - FIX: phase2-ai could strand a rebuild when Azure AI Search landed in a terminal
           'Failed' provisioningState (a regional capacity blip during allocation). Because the
           Search name is deterministic and phase2 deploys in Incremental mode, ARM REUSED the
           Failed resource, so both in-run retries AND every fresh `build.sh` failed identically
           ("ResourceDeploymentFailure ... terminal provisioning state 'Failed'" on
           srch-rmx-<suffix>) until it was deleted by hand -- previously needing a full wipe.
           infra/phase2-ai/up.sh now runs a _heal_failed_search guard at the top of each
           deployment attempt: it deletes a Search stuck in failed/canceled state (by its
           deterministic name) so the attempt recreates it clean, while leaving a healthy
           (Succeeded) or still-provisioning Search untouched for reuse. AI Search stays in
           AZ_REGION_SEARCH (default centralindia -- the reliable India Search region; South
           India is capacity-constrained), baked in with no runtime export required. Infra-only
           -- no data / answer / nudge changes.
