  v2.1.5 - FIX: rebuild after a wipe failed at the preflight gate with a SILENT "phase3 exit 1"
           ("Generate and validate deterministic datasets (exit 1)", no error text). Two-part bug:
           * ROOT CAUSE: the wipe (wipe-parallel.sh -> phase3-data/down.sh) ran `rm -rf data/csv`,
             treating the CSV pack as GENERATED. But data/csv is a COMMITTED, deterministic pack that
             ships with the repo; phase3-data/up.sh only VALIDATES it (validate_seed.py) and never
             regenerates it. So after one wipe the pack was gone and every rebuild failed. FIX:
             phase3-data/down.sh no longer deletes data/csv — Phase 3 creates no Azure resources, so
             teardown is now a no-op that PRESERVES data/csv, data/knowledge_base and docs/sop (all
             committed artifacts). Wipe -> rebuild is now idempotent.
           * ERROR-SURFACING: phase3-data/up.sh line ~22 computed CSV_COUNT via
             `find data/csv ... | wc -l` under `set -euo pipefail`; when data/csv was missing, find
             exited non-zero and pipefail aborted the script BEFORE the friendly
             "No CSVs found under data/csv" die — hence the silent exit 1. Hardened with
             `{ find ... || true; }` so a missing pack now yields the clear die message instead.
           RECOVERY for an already-wiped VM (restores only data/csv, keeps your env.sh):
             cd ~ && tar -xzf <your-tarball>.tar.gz -C ~ contoso-retail-rm-assist-rakesh/data/csv
  v2.1.4 - REWRITE: ACS-Teams-Live-Video-Integration.md is now a no-npm, HTTPS-correct guide.
           Motivation: a plain http://<vm-ip>:8080 origin is NOT a browser "secure context", so
           getUserMedia (camera/mic) is blocked and the Teams call cannot send video; http://localhost
           only works if the browser runs on the same box (an Azure VM has no webcam/desktop). The
           guide no longer uses Node.js/npm/webpack/Express at all. Instead:
           * The client is a SINGLE static index.html; the ACS Calling Web SDK is loaded straight from
             a CDN as browser ESM (jsdelivr /+esm for @azure/communication-calling@1.43.1, which
             resolves @azure/logger + @azure/communication-common automatically) inside a
             <script type="module"> — nothing to install or build.
           * It is hosted on an Azure Storage STATIC WEBSITE, which serves the page over real HTTPS
             (https://<acct>.z<nn>.web.core.windows.net) — a secure context, so the camera works from
             any webcam machine (your laptop). The static endpoint is anonymous and unaffected by the
             account's "allow blob public access" flag, so it survives lock-down policies.
           * The VoIP token is minted with `az communication identity token issue --scope voip` and
             pasted into the page (two inputs: Teams meeting link + token) — so the deployed file holds
             NO secrets and there is no token server.
           * Provisioning (ACS + storage static website), upload, token, and teardown are all `az`;
             every value is a variable at the top (RG/LOCATION/ACS_NAME/ACS_DATA_LOCATION/STORAGE_NAME).
             Added an explicit HTTP-vs-HTTPS section, a "multiple guests in parallel" section, and
             updated troubleshooting. No demo code changed; this is a doc-only release.
