  v2.1.2 - FIX: `wipe.sh` (default, keep-the-RG per-phase teardown) could leave the PAYG chat
           deployment (gpt-4.1-mini-payg) behind. Root cause: wipe.sh does not remember the
           build's --type, so DEPLOY_TYPE defaults to 'ptu' on a bare `wipe.sh` and phase2/down.sh's
           fast per-deployment delete targeted gpt-4.1-mini-ptu (absent) instead of the actual
           gpt-4.1-mini-payg — leaving it (and its billing) to rely solely on the account-cascade.
           phase2/down.sh now ENUMERATES and deletes EVERY model deployment on the account (chat
           ptu AND payg, plus embedding) regardless of --type, before the account delete, so billing
           stops immediately and nothing is orphaned. Names listed in AOAI_CHAT_PROTECTED_DEPLOYMENTS
           (empty by default) are still skipped. Also removed a stale "KV secrets" line and the unused
           _dep_delete_note helper from the phase2 teardown preview (Key Vault was removed in v2.1.0).
  v2.1.1 - FIX: embedding deployment failed in South India with InvalidResourceProperties
           "The specified SKU 'Standard' for model 'text-embedding-3-small 1' is not supported
           in this region 'southindia'." In southindia text-embedding-3-small is offered ONLY as
           GlobalStandard (verified via `az cognitiveservices model list -l southindia`), while the
           plain 'Standard' SKU is not. Changed AOAI_EMBED_SKU_NAME default from 'Standard' ->
           'GlobalStandard' in env.sh (GlobalStandard is also valid in the usual PTU regions, so it
           is the portable default; still overridable per region). No other changes; the chat model
           already used GlobalStandard/GlobalProvisionedManaged and was unaffected.
  v2.1.0 - REMOVED Azure Key Vault from the stack entirely, making the build immune to
           subscription Azure Policies that force Key Vault publicNetworkAccess=Disabled
           (the "Public network access is disabled ... ForbiddenByConnection" failures that
           blocked build_rg.sh and the runtime container apps):
           * No vault is created and the deployer never touches a vault data plane. Every app
             secret (Tool API bearer token, Foundry/Search/ACS endpoints + connection strings)
             is now a LITERAL Container App secret — passed as @secure() Bicep params (phase4,
             phase6) or `az containerapp secret set` (phase9) — and carried between phases via
             each phase's outputs.env file (the existing transport).
           * phase1 main.bicep/up.sh/down.sh: dropped the KV resource, its two role assignments
             (Key Vault Administrator / Secrets User), the kvName param and kvId/kvUri outputs,
             and the _del_kv teardown.
           * phase2 main.bicep/up.sh/down.sh: removed the keyVaultName param, the existing-vault
             reference, all 11 Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets resources and the _set_kv writes;
             SEARCH_INDEX_NAME + the Foundry/Search/ACS wiring values are emitted to outputs.env.
           * phase4: 10 new @secure() params feed literal secret values (bearer generated ONCE in
             up.sh and persisted to outputs.env); phase5/6/9 read the bearer from phase4 outputs.env.
           * setup_docker_cache.sh: the KV-backed ACR credential-set + cache rule is replaced by an
             authenticated `az acr import` (inline Docker Hub creds) of the nginx base image.
           * env.sh: removed NAME_KV, the heal_keyvault_public_access helper, the KV_PROBE_STRICT
             knob, and all KV_URI handling in regen_phase1_outputs / assert_foundation_present.
           * phase0 no longer registers Microsoft.KeyVault; wipe no longer purges a soft-deleted
             vault. README gained a "Key Vault-free by design" section (replacing "Locked-down Key
             Vault"); every value stays configurable in env.sh. No other resource shapes changed.
  v2.0.2 - SPLIT the build into three scripts so RG-level, non-billable setup runs ONCE and
           the teardown no longer deletes the resource group by default:
           * build_rg.sh (NEW, run once) — BUILD_STAGE=foundation: creates the resource group
             + Phase-1 platform (Log Analytics, ACR, UAMI, Container Apps env), then stops.
             Non-billable (ACR Basic ~$5/mo is the only standing cost).
           * build.sh (NEW, per demo) — BUILD_STAGE=apps: provisions the billable stack
             (phases 2-9) assuming the foundation exists; keeps `--type=ptu|payg`. Asserts the
             foundation is present and rehydrates phase1 outputs.env from Azure if missing, so
             it runs even in a fresh shell / re-extracted tarball.
           * wipe.sh — DEFAULT CHANGED to keep the RG: now runs the per-phase teardown with
             WIPE_DELETE_RG=0 + KEEP_PLATFORM=1 (deletes the billable stack, KEEPS the RG +
             platform). `wipe.sh --delete-rg` (or WIPE_DELETE_RG=1) restores the full
             all-or-nothing RG delete + soft-delete purge.
           * deploy.sh unchanged as the one-shot (BUILD_STAGE=all = build_rg + build combined);
             final message + header updated for the new wipe default.
           * NEW env.sh helpers: assert_foundation_present, regen_phase1_outputs.
             New knob: BUILD_STAGE (all|foundation|apps).
           * rebuild-parallel.sh staged into foundation vs apps portions by BUILD_STAGE.
           * README documents the 3-script model. No resource shapes changed; every value stays
             configurable in env.sh.
  v2.0.1 - FIX: standalone Speech (SpeechServices kind) is not offered in South India — ARM
           rejected phase2 with InvalidApiSetId "account type 'SpeechServices' is unavailable
           in given region". The Speech account now has its own region, AZ_REGION_SPEECH
