           account in AZ_REGION_SPEECH. No other behavior changed.
  v2.0.0 - SELF-CONTAINED, ALL-OR-NOTHING build. Nothing pre-existing is reused; the stack
           now CREATES its own resource group in South India and provisions EVERYTHING inside
           it, and `wipe.sh` DELETES the whole resource group. Changes:
           * New resource group (AZ_RG, default rg-contoso-rmx-rakesh) is CREATED by phase0 and
             DELETED on wipe. Default region AZ_REGION=southindia; AI Search region overridable
             via AZ_REGION_SEARCH (default centralindia for capacity headroom).
           * phase2 now CREATES the Azure AI Foundry (AIServices) account + project via Bicep
             (was: discover a pre-existing one), then CLI-creates BOTH the chat deployment and
             the text-embedding-3-small embedding deployment on it (auto-discovers the latest
             model version, overridable via env). ACS gets a system-assigned identity so the
             transcription role grant works on a freshly-created ACS.
           * `--type` now picks how the chat model is CREATED (both are created + deleted):
               --type=ptu  (default) -> gpt-4.1-mini-ptu  (GlobalProvisionedManaged, 15 PTU)
               --type=payg           -> gpt-4.1-mini-payg (GlobalStandard, pay-as-you-go)
           * wipe.sh -> `az group delete` on the whole RG, then purges the soft-deleted
             Cognitive Services accounts (AIServices + Speech) and Key Vault so the globally
             unique names are immediately reusable. Safety: refuses to delete an RG that lacks
             this project's tag unless WIPE_FORCE=1. Optional per-phase teardown that keeps the
             empty RG shell via WIPE_DELETE_RG=0. Async delete via WIPE_RG_NOWAIT=1.
           * Every value remains configurable in infra/common/env.sh — no hardcoded resource
             IDs; all names derive from a deterministic suffix.
  v1.0.5 - Faster deploy & wipe (all opt-in via env vars, safe fallback = old behavior).
           DEPLOY: PREBUILD_IMAGES=1 (default) builds the three container images
           (Tool API, Video Assist, CRM dashboard) CONCURRENTLY in the background right
           after phase1, overlapping them with phase2's slow AI Search provisioning; phases
           4/6/9 then reuse the ready images instead of building serially across later waves.
           If a pre-build fails, that phase falls back to building inline. PHASE5_REBUILD_TOOLAPI=0
           (default) skips phase5's redundant Tool API image rebuild — phase4's image already
           contains rag.py/search.py and RAG is read at runtime, so no redeploy is needed
           (set =1 to force it). WIPE: WIPE_PARALLEL_DELETES=1 (default) tears down independent
           resources concurrently. Escape hatches: PREBUILD_IMAGES=0, PHASE5_REBUILD_TOOLAPI=1,
           WIPE_PARALLEL_DELETES=0; existing KEEP_PLATFORM=1 still skips the slow phase1 teardown.
